# p_4e7a — Priya's Photography Walks; Camera Leaves the House on Errands

Priya is retired and photography is one of her main hobbies alongside board games and yoga. Her camera rests on the bookshelf in the living room when she is not using it. On weekday mornings she takes a walk (roughly 7:00–9:00) and on weekday afternoons she runs errands (roughly 14:00–16:00). On weekends she takes a late-morning walk (roughly 10:00–12:00). During these outings she carries the camera to photograph the neighbourhood, the dog, or whatever catches her eye. The camera is therefore OUT_OF_HOUSE during those windows and back on the bookshelf the rest of the time. This hypothesis differs from p_c9d4 and p_a3f7, which keep the camera on the bookshelf all week; here the camera is out for 2–3 hours at a stretch. If the robot ever sees camera_priya on the bookshelf during a weekday 7–9 h window, or during a weekend 10–12 h window, that refutes this document.

