# p_8b1d — Hana's Late-Night Wind-Down; Snack, TV, Bed by Midnight

Hana works afternoon-to-night shifts and gets home around 23:00 on weekdays. She is tired and wants to snack and watch a little TV before going to bed. She grabs a snack from the snack bowl (which lives in the kitchen cupboard between uses), pulls the blanket from the coffee table, and settles on the couch with the remote. She watches for about 30–45 minutes, then heads to bed (bed_b1) by roughly 00:00–00:30. On weekends she is home all day and this late-night routine does not apply. This document differs from p_789a (which has Hana cooking at midnight) and p_c3d4 (which has her doing separate evenings with no shared TV). Here there is no cooking after 23:00; it is snacking and TV only. If the robot finds the pan on the counter at 23:30 or finds Hana's plate at the dining table at 23:30, this document is refuted. If the remote is never on the coffee table after 23:00, the TV claim weakens.

